# Never let a real secret or the local dev database into ANY image's build
# context — a Dockerfile that COPYs a whole component directory (api/web/
# deploy-agent) would otherwise bake .env's JWT secret, LDAP bind password,
# break-glass password, and (as of INIT-0035) DEPLOY_AGENT_TOKEN straight into
# an image layer, plus the encrypted-store master key and databases if a dev
# checkout's .data/ happens to be present in the build context (security
# review, 2026-08-21 — this file never existed before, a pre-existing gap the
# deploy-agent work made materially worse by adding a new secret and a new
# powerful permission a leaked JWT secret could forge).
# Unlike .gitignore, a .dockerignore pattern with no `**/` prefix matches ONLY
# at the build-context root (Docker's documented behavior) — every Dockerfile
# here declares the REPO ROOT as build context, but the real secret file is
# nested at components/api/.env, not the root, so the first version of this
# file (root-only `.env`/`.env.*`) matched nothing at all (caught on a second
# security-gate pass, 2026-08-21, after the first version shipped with this
# exact bug). `**/` matches at any depth.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/.data/
node_modules
.git
# The extension signing key (decisions/0002 non-negotiable: never in the
# CRX or git). No current Dockerfile copies components/browser-extension/.keys/,
# and it's gitignored, so this isn't an active leak today — but a later
# `COPY . .` would ship it silently without this (third security-gate pass,
# 2026-08-21).
**/.keys/
**/*.pem
